### Describe the bug

The analyzer for CA2241 does not identify call-sites passing invalid composite-format-string arguments when the call-site's target method is an extension-method using the new C# 14.0 `extension()` syntax; whereas the analyzer does report CA2241 when using the old `static` syntax).

(This is not a duplicate of https://github.com/dotnet/sdk/issues/57258, which concerns false-_positives_ caused by `IFormatProvider` parameters in the old `static` syntax)

### Steps to reproduce

## Repro.cs:

```
global using StrSyn = global::System.Diagnostics.CodeAnalysis.StringSyntaxAttribute;

using System;
using System.Globalization;
using System.Runtime.CompilerServices;

public class Program
{
	public static void Main()
	{
		// Without IFormatProvider:

		// No CA2241 warning is generated when it should (4 args for 3 placeholders):
		_ = @"Arg0: {0}, Arg1: {1}, Arg2: {2}".FmtExt( "arg0", 1, 2.0, 3.0 );

		// No CA2241 warning is generated when it should (3 args for 4 placeholders):
		_ = @"Arg0: {0}, Arg1: {1}, Arg2: {2}, Arg3: {3}".FmtExt( "arg0", 1, 2.0 );

		// With IFormatProvider:

		// No CA2241 warning is generated when it should (4 args for 3 placeholders):
		_ = @"Arg0: {0}, Arg1: {1}, Arg2: {2}".FmtExtP( CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, "arg0", 1, 2.0, 3.0 );

		// No CA2241 warning is generated when it should (3 args for 4 placeholders):
		_ = @"Arg0: {0}, Arg1: {1}, Arg2: {2}, Arg3: {3}".FmtExtP( CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, "arg0", 1, 2.0 );
	}
}

internal static class Consts
{
	public const MethodImplOptions Inline = MethodImplOptions.AggressiveInlining | MethodImplOptions.AggressiveOptimization;
}

public static class CSharp14StringFormatExtensions_NoIFormatProvider
{
	extension( [StrSyn( StrSyn.CompositeFormat )] String format )
	{
#pragma warning disable CA1305 // Specify IFormatProvider

			/// <summary>Calls <see cref="String.Format( String, Object)"/>.</summary>
			[MethodImpl( Consts.Inline )]
			public String FmtExt( Object? arg0 )
			{
				return String.Format( format: format, arg0: arg0 );
			}

			/// <summary>Calls <see cref="String.Format( String, Object, Object)"/>.</summary>
			[MethodImpl( Consts.Inline )]
			public String FmtExt( Object? arg0, Object? arg1 )
			{
				return String.Format( format: format, arg0: arg0, arg1 );
			}

			/// <summary>Calls <see cref="String.Format( String, Object, Object, Object)"/>.</summary>
			[MethodImpl( Consts.Inline )]
			public String FmtExt( Object? arg0, Object? arg1, Object? arg2 )
			{
				return String.Format( format: format, arg0: arg0, arg1, arg2 );
			}

			/// <summary>Calls <see cref="String.Format( String, Object[])"/>.</summary>
			[MethodImpl( Consts.Inline )]
			public String FmtExt( params Object?[]? args )
			{
				return String.Format( format: format, args: args ?? Array.Empty<Object?>() );
			}

#pragma warning restore CA1305 // Specify IFormatProvider
	}
}

public static class CSharp14StringFormatExtensions_WithIFormatProvider
{
		extension( [StrSyn( StrSyn.CompositeFormat )] String format )
		{
			/// <summary>Calls <see cref="String.Format(IFormatProvider, String, Object)"/>.</summary>
			[MethodImpl( Consts.Inline )]
			public String FmtExtP( IFormatProvider? formatProvider, Object? arg0 )
			{
				return String.Format( provider: formatProvider, format, arg0 );
			}

			/// <summary>Calls <see cref="String.Format(IFormatProvider, String, Object, Object)"/>.</summary>
			[MethodImpl( Consts.Inline )]
			public String FmtExtP( IFormatProvider? formatProvider, Object? arg0, Object? arg1 )
			{
				return String.Format( provider: formatProvider, format, arg0, arg1 );
			}

			/// <summary>Calls <see cref="String.Format(IFormatProvider, String, Object, Object, Object)"/>.</summary>
			[MethodImpl( Consts.Inline )]
			public String FmtExtP( IFormatProvider? formatProvider, Object? arg0, Object? arg1, Object? arg2 )
			{
				return String.Format( provider: formatProvider, format, arg0, arg1, arg2 );
			}

			/// <summary>Calls <see cref="String.Format(IFormatProvider, String, Object[])"/>.</summary>
			[MethodImpl( Consts.Inline )]
			public String FmtExtP( IFormatProvider? formatProvider, params Object?[]? args )
			{
				return String.Format( provider: formatProvider, format, args: args ?? Array.Empty<Object?>() );
			}
	}
}
```

### Expected behavior

I expected four CA2241 warnings, as listed in the `Program.Main` comments.

### Actual behavior

No warnings/diagnostics were reported, despite the call-site arguments being invalid for the format-string's placeholders.

### Is this a regression?

N/A. The new `extension()` syntax is new to .NET 10.0.

### Are there any workarounds?

Some extension-methods can be rewritten in the old style, but this means losing out on the new extension syntax features, especially for open-generics.

